Your taglines.atp and atprc belong in your home directory.Alternatively, you can setup another directory by setting theenvironment variable ATP to point somewhere else.Edit atprc to tell ATP about your editor, file archiver and otheroptions.Suggested settings for the atprc variables "charset" and "graphics":Table 1. Character Set Options for atprc Variables---------------------------------------------------          |    charset      |     graphics          |                 |Linux     |    latin1       |       on          |                 |386bsd    |    msdos        |       off               |                 | VT100     |    7bit         |       on          |                 |generic   |    7bit         |       off           |                 |             MS-DOS    |    msdos        |       off          |                 |-------------------------------------------------- Don't forget that you will need an archiver to packand unpack messages. For compatibility with the mostBBS you should choose Info-Zip's UNZIP 5.0 and ZIP 1.0.These are available in source code form. Try Mac's PlaceBBS (919) 891-1111. Do *NOT* use ZIP 1.9 becasue thisuses the "deflation" method which is incompatible withmost BBS zip archivers. Invoke zip/unzip with the -jswitch which will junk the path information from thearchives.